  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nIsolated to scattered showers and a few thunderstorms are expected\nto continue through this morning as southwest flow aloft persists.\nWith short term ensembles keeping up to 700 J/kg of CAPE around \nand 25-35 kts of bulk shear, a few strong thunderstorms are \npossible during the afternoon. With showers around through the \nmorning, this may limit the strength of the thunderstorms expected\nto develop during the afternoon. The main threat with any \nstronger thunderstorms will be gusty winds and brief heavy rain. \nInto Sunday, as troughing approaches, an associated cold front \nwill bring scattered showers and thunderstorms with cool and \nbreezy conditions to follow. Hi-res models show precipitation \nassociated with the front moving through south central MT during \nthe early morning hours. With little instability around in the \nmorning, only a few weak thunderstorms are expected. A few \nstronger thunderstorms are possible across southeast MT as daytime\nheating allows for instability to increase. There is some \ndisagreeance on additional thunderstorms behind the main push, but\nthis will depend on the subsidence behind the front. With this \nsubsidence, breezy conditions with wind gusts in the 30s (mph) are\nexpected across south central MT. Additionally, cooler \ntemperatures in the Crazy and Beartooth mountains will allow for \nmoderate chances for snow Sunday morning. Up to a couple inches \nare possible at the highest peaks (above 10,000 ft). Plan ahead if\nyou have plans to recreate in the high country. \n\nEnsembles depict brief ridging building in for Monday, allowing\nfor recovery from cooler temperatures and precipitation. \nSouthwest flow aloft begins to build in Tuesday through the \nremainder of the week as troughing sits over the Pacific \nnorthwest. This looks to bring small chances for showers and \nthunderstorms at least for Tuesday and Wednesday. \n\nHigh temperatures will be in the 70s and 80s today, cooling to the\n70s and low 80s Sunday. Temperatures will rebound by midweek into\nthe upper 70s and 80s. TS",
